# Level 9 over the same tree as `phpstan.neon.dist`, reported only for the
# classes that read rows out of `$wpdb`.
#
# Why a second config instead of raising the level of the first one: level 9
# reports every mishandled `mixed` in the repository — 2948 of them when this
# file was written, and 92% of those have nothing to do with the database
# (`$_POST`, `get_option()`, `json_decode()`, hook arguments). Raising the
# main gate would mean baselining thousands of errors in bulk, which trades a
# specific blindness for a generic suppression.
#
# Why the tree is NOT restricted to the row-reading files: measured, because
# it is tempting and wrong. Narrowing `paths` to the 45 files takes the rest
# of `includes/` out of the analysis, so PHPStan loses the inferred return
# types of everything they call and invents `mixed` that does not exist —
# 778 errors instead of 243, with `scanDirectories` bringing it only to 363.
# Chasing that gap would mean annotating things that are not defects. The
# whole tree is analysed; `.github/scripts/phpstan-rows-report.php` is what
# narrows the report.
#
# See rpgmem/ffcertificate#1060.

includes:
    - phpstan.neon.dist

parameters:
    level: 9
